<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>media3 on onseok</title><link>https://onseok.github.io/tags/media3/</link><description>Recent content in media3 on onseok</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><copyright>© {year} onseok</copyright><lastBuildDate>Tue, 24 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0900</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://onseok.github.io/tags/media3/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>The Subtitle Rendering Pipeline in AndroidX Media3</title><link>https://onseok.github.io/posts/media3-subtitle-deep-dive/</link><pubDate>Tue, 24 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0900</pubDate><guid>https://onseok.github.io/posts/media3-subtitle-deep-dive/</guid><description>&lt;style&gt;
.pf { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; margin: 1.5em 0; }
.pf .ar { opacity: 0.5; font-size: 1.2em; }
.pb { padding: 10px 14px; border: 1.5px solid var(--text-color); border-radius: 6px; text-align: center; font-size: 0.9em; min-width: 100px; }
.pb .num { font-size: 0.75em; opacity: 0.6; display: block; }
.pb .detail { font-size: 0.8em; opacity: 0.7; margin-top: 2px; }
.cg { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; margin: 1.5em 0; }
@media (max-width: 500px) { .cg { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
.cc { border: 1.5px solid var(--text-color); border-radius: 6px; padding: 14px; }
.cc.green { border-left: 4px solid #4caf50; }
.cc.orange { border-left: 4px solid #ff9800; }
.cc h4 { margin: 0 0 6px; color: var(--heading-color); }
.cc .tag { font-size: 0.8em; opacity: 0.6; }
.cc ul { margin: 8px 0 0; padding-left: 18px; font-size: 0.9em; line-height: 1.6; }
.sc { margin: 1.5em 0; padding: 14px 16px; border: 1.5px solid var(--text-color); border-left: 4px solid var(--link-color); border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0; font-size: 0.92em; line-height: 1.7; }
.tl { margin: 1.5em 0; font-size: 0.85em; }
.tl-row { display: flex; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 6px; }
.tl-lbl { width: 60px; opacity: 0.7; flex-shrink: 0; }
.tl-track { flex: 1; position: relative; height: 24px; }
.tl-bar { position: absolute; height: 100%; border-radius: 4px; border: 1.5px solid var(--text-color); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: bold; }
.tl-vis { flex: 1; height: 28px; display: flex; }
.tl-seg { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: bold; font-size: 0.9em; border: 1px solid var(--text-color); }
.tl-seg:first-child { border-radius: 4px 0 0 4px; }
.tl-seg:last-child { border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0; }
.db { border: 1.5px solid var(--text-color); border-radius: 8px; padding: 16px; margin: 1.5em 0; }
.db-title { font-weight: bold; text-align: center; margin-bottom: 12px; color: var(--heading-color); }
figcaption { color: var(--text-color); opacity: 0.8; text-align: center; font-size: 0.85em; margin-top: 8px; }
&lt;/style&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have you ever wondered what happens between the moment a subtitle file is downloaded and the text appears at the bottom of your video? In AndroidX Media3 (the successor to ExoPlayer), the answer involves a surprisingly deep pipeline of parsers, encoders, resolvers, and renderers.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>